        "props": {
          "style": {
            "classes": "kanoa/font/default",
            "fontSize": "12px",
            "paddingLeft": "5px",
            "whiteSpace": "normal"
          },
          "text": "Cycle rate: how many times a minute or hour the machine cycles with this tool (shots, strokes). An item\u0027s standard rate is the cycle rate x its parts per cycle, from the tool\u0027s positions set to that item or to no item, x the package count of the machine\u0027s rate for the item (parts are outfeed units; the standard rate is in the rate\u0027s infeed units, so a 0.1 lb part with a package count of 0.1 makes 0.1 lb a part) (blocked positions count: the parts they aren\u0027t making show as a performance loss; retired ones don\u0027t). An item with its own rate for this tool (Configuration \u003e Ops \u003e Materials, Production Rates: edit the machine\u0027s rate for the item and pick the tool) uses that instead; with neither, the machine\u0027s item rate is used."
        },
        "type": "ia.display.label"
      },
